  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "This year ppp footballers and qqq cricketers have been invited to participate in IPL (Indian Programming League) as guests. You have to accommodate them in rrr rooms such that:\n\n\nNo room may remain empty.\nA room may contain either only footballers or only cricketers, not both.\nNo cricketers are allowed to stay alone in a room.\nFind the number of ways to place the players. Note though, that all the rooms are identical. But each of the cricketers and footballers are unique.\n\nSince the number of ways can be very large, print the answer modulo 998,244,353998,244,353998,244,353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains three space-separated integers ppp, qqq and rrr denoting the number of footballers, cricketers and rooms.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the number of ways to place the players modulo 998,244,353998,244,353998,244,353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤p,q,r≤1001 \\le p, q, r \\le 1001≤p,q,r≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n2 1 4\n2 4 4\n2 5 4\n2 8 4",
        "output": "0\n3\n10\n609",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 2: Three possible ways are:\n\n{Footballer 1}, {Footballer 2}, {Cricketer 1, Cricketer 2}, {Cricketer 3, Cricketer 4}\n{Footballer 1}, {Footballer 2}, {Cricketer 1, Cricketer 3}, {Cricketer 2, Cricketer 4}\n{Footballer 1}, {Footballer 2}, {Cricketer 1, Cricketer 4}, {Cricketer 2, Cricketer 3}\n\nPlease note that the rooms are identical."
      }
    ]
  },
